<title>USA: Fannie Mae to redeem $450 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae to redeem $450 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fannie Mae on Wednesday said that on August 8 it will redeem all outstanding amounts of six medium-term note issues totalling $450 million as follows.</p>
<p>  Principal     Interest    Maturity    Cusip</p>
<p>   Amount	   Rate	  Date	Number</p>
<p> $100 million     6.69	07/28/00   31364BGJ3</p>
<p> $100 million     7.43	07/22/05   31364BGB0</p>
<p> $100 million     7.39	07/29/05   31364BGD6</p>
<p>  $50 million     6.15	11/06/98   31364BPC8</p>
<p>  $50 million     6.28	03/18/99   31364BZH6</p>
<p>  $50 million     6.82	03/27/01   31364BA91</p>
<p>The redemption price of the notes will be 100 percent of the principal amount plus interest accrued to the redemption date, Fannie Mae said.</p>
</text>
